--TEST--
require-features pointing at a package nothing requires is reported instead of silently ignored
--COMPOSER--
{
    "repositories": [
        {
            "type": "package",
            "package": [
                { "name": "a/a", "version": "1.0.0" },
                { "name": "y/unused", "version": "1.0.0", "features": { "x": { "require": { "c/c": "1.0.0" } } } },
                { "name": "c/c", "version": "1.0.0" }
            ]
        }
    ],
    "require": {
        "a/a": "1.0.0"
    },
    "require-features": {
        "y/unused": ["x"]
    }
}
--RUN--
update
--EXPECT-OUTPUT--
Loading composer repositories with package information
<warning>Warning: Root composer.json requires feature x of y/unused, but y/unused is not required by anything so this is ignored.</warning>
Updating dependencies
Lock file operations: 1 install, 0 updates, 0 removals
  - Locking a/a (1.0.0)
Writing lock file
Installing dependencies from lock file (including require-dev)
Package operations: 1 install, 0 updates, 0 removals
Generating autoload files

--EXPECT--
Installing a/a (1.0.0)
